1️⃣ Scenario: Consumer crashes after processing message

Question

A Kafka consumer processes a payment event but crashes before committing the offset. Kafka sends the message again. How do you prevent duplicate processing?

Answer

Kafka provides at-least-once delivery, so duplicates are possible.

Solution:

Make the consumer idempotent

Store transaction_id/event_id

Check before processing

Example logic:

Receive message
      ↓
Check transaction_id in DB
      ↓
If exists → ignore
Else → process
